---
description: Coding rules
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---
* Do not write code unless explicitly asked
* Prefer minimal implementations to overengineered and "future-proof" code. YAGNI.
* Avoid superfluous and excessive commenting of the code; make the actual code legible instead
* Attempt to write idiomatic code
* Ignore architectural rules, for example, modularity, backward compatibility, etc. unless working on larger projects
